      entry_arm="$entry_arm - **and this is NOT any of those arms either: it is 844's STORAGE arm, RUNG 49 - THE MBR PARTITION TABLE DECODED FROM THE SECTOR THE READ ALREADY MOVED** (STAGE90_XNU_STORAGE_PROBE=48, VALUE 48 = ORDINAL RUNG 49 - the switch counts the VALUE and the arm counts the RUNG, one apart - resolved set \`${SET:-<unresolved>}\`). **IT IS THE RUNG-48 PRESS'S OWN FRONTIER AND IT ADDS NO COMMAND, NO REGISTER, NO WINDOW AND NO BYTE OF THE MEDIUM**: the rung-48 press (844) measured the signature - \`_rd_mbr = 1\` with \`_rd_sig = 0xAA55\` - so **the medium is MBR-partitioned**, and the four 16-byte partition records at bytes 446-509 of LBA 0 are ALREADY in \`st_read_block\`. **Rung 49 is a body that READS that buffer and nothing else**: \`st_mbr_parse\`, called ONCE after \`st_read_single_block\`, which makes NO device access at all - a fact the build clause makes STRUCTURAL (every \`bl\` in its body is to \`entry_live_write\`, the cell-publisher, and a body containing any other callee is REFUSED). **THE RECORD IS NOT WORD-ALIGNED, AND THAT IS THE ONE WAY THIS PARSE GOES WRONG SILENTLY**: \`446 = 4*111 + 2\`, so each record's byte 0 is the HIGH half of word \`111+4k\` (the boot flag) and its TYPE byte is the high half of word \`112+4k\`, while the two 32-bit fields the standard puts at bytes 8-11 and 12-15 ARE word-aligned at \`113+4k\` and \`114+4k\` and read little-endian with NO swizzle. A parser that took the type from a word's low byte, or byte-reversed the LBA word, would read a plausible but WRONG number and every cell would still read as success. **READ THE ROWS AS THE ARM'S OWN TABLE.** \`_pm_sig_ok = 1\` is **THE SECTOR IS AN MBR AND THE WALK BELOW IS A TABLE** - the module re-checks \`0xAA55\` itself rather than trusting rung 48's cell, so \`_pm_sig_ok = 0\` beside \`_rd_complete = 1\` is a sector the walk refused to treat as an MBR (a stale or gated read left the buffer holding something else) and the four cells below are NOT a partition table. \`_pm_nonzero = 1\` names the FIRST record whose type byte is not zero - the first real partition - with \`_pm_index\` saying WHICH of the four it was (3 is a different medium from 0), and \`_pm_nonzero_type\`/\`_pm_nonzero_first\`/\`_pm_nonzero_len\` giving that partition's type code and its first LBA and length: **\`_pm_nonzero_first\` is the sector the next rung reads**. \`_pm_entries = 4\` is the walk's own bound and \`_pm_p0_*\` is entry 0's record whatever it is (an all-zero entry 0 with a non-zero entry 1 is a protective or aligned table). \`_pm_nonzero\` ABSENT with \`_pm_done = 1\` is **A TABLE WITH NO NON-ZERO TYPE** - a protective-only MBR (a GPT disk's LBA 0 keeps one 0xEE entry) or an empty one, which would move the frontier back to the medium's layout rather than forward. **\`build_entry.sh\`'s clause \`xnu_entry_844\` refuses the build** unless \`st_mbr_parse\`'s linked body calls NOTHING BUT \`entry_live_write\`, materializes 43605 = \`0xAA55\` (the signature re-check), and is called ONCE by \`st_cmd_path\` AFTER the \`bl <st_read_single_block>\` - so a body that quietly issued a command, that walked the table without re-checking the signature, or that ran on a stale buffer, is REFUSED. **IT MOVES NO BYTE OF THE MEDIUM AND TOUCHES NO DEVICE REGISTER**: the medium is not touched at all - this rung is a decode of bytes the previous rung's read already landed. The entry-group page move did NOT fire (\`STAGE90_XNU_SEAM_LR\` stays \`0x8004c2dc\`). \`STAGE90_XNU_PWR_WAIT_TICKS=384000\` is inherited from rung 9 unchanged - 20 ms at this device's own 19,200,000 Hz. \`fastboot boot\` only; nothing flashed. **NO PRESS HAS BEEN MADE AND NONE IS OWED: this arm is PARKED and NOT ARMED-FOR-PRESS, and the park is a RECORD and not a queue. THE PRESS IS THE OPERATOR'S.** **THE GOAL IS NOT MET** - no partition's sector read, no filesystem, no mount; TWRP-to-storage stays withheld."
