    rung_para 31 " **THIS RUNG HAS BEEN PRESSED AND ITS ANSWER REFUTED ITS OWN MECHANISM: THE REGISTER WAS RAISED EIGHTFOLD, THE BLOCK HELD THE NEW VALUE, AND THE TIMEOUT FIRED AT THE SAME INSTANT.** 2026-09-28 08:12-08:13 UTC, EXIT 0; \`_tout_was = 0\` (the register held zero, the reset value, as predicted), \`_tout_held = 3\`, \`_tout_wrote_back = 0\`, \`_tout_readback = 0\` - the store landed and was undone. \`_cid_ticks\` 12,772 = 665.3 us against rung 31's 12,770 = 665.2 us under a bound EIGHT TIMES longer, with \`_cid_status_any = 0x00018000\` (\`ERR | TIMEOUT\`) and \`_cid_complete = 0\` on both. **So \`TIMEOUT_CONTROL 0x2E\` does not govern this event** - the spec's timeout register scales the DATA timeout, the command response timeout is fixed in the block - and **the card is not answering at all**, which is why 795 section 5's extrapolation stands untested. **AND THE PRESS HANDED OVER THE REAL FINDING, WHICH IS NOT ABOUT A REGISTER: CMD1 IS SENT ONCE WHERE THE DRIVER LOOPS, AND THE GATE BELOW IT READS THE DRIVER'S OWN TEST BACKWARDS.** \`mmc_ops.c:157\` is \`if (cmd.resp[0] & MMC_CARD_BUSY) break;\` - the driver PROCEEDS WHEN BIT 31 SETS - while \`entry_storage.c:4702\` sends CMD1 a single time and \`:4785\` proceeds when bit 31 is CLEAR. \`_cmd1_resp = 0x40ff8080\` has bit 31 CLEAR, so **the driver's loop would have retried 99 more times** and this ladder went on to CMD2. **So CMD2 is put on the bus for a card that has never reported power-up complete, and the card does not answer.** CMD1 IS answered - because a card answers CMD1 while it initializes, which is what the retry loop is for. **THE NEXT ARM IS THE FIRST TIME THIS LADDER PORTS THE DRIVER'S OWN CONTROL FLOW**: the \`mmc_send_op_cond\` loop, with two new cells - how many sends it took and whether the bit ever set. **AND 796's OWN PROSE IS REFUTED BY THIS PRESS**: its guard is \`>= 30\`, so rung 32 inherited rung 31's CRC-dropped word and sent \`0x0201\`, not \`0x0209\` as the record claimed. THIS RUNG IS THE FIRST REPAIR THIS LADDER HAS MADE, AND ITS SUBJECT IS A REGISTER THAT HAS BEEN SITTING AT ITS RESET VALUE SINCE THE FIRST PRESS.** 795 read rung 31's own capture and found that the 665.2 us CMD2 and CMD3 both hit - and that CMD1 completes 130 us inside - is not a property of the card: it is \`TIMEOUT_CONTROL 0x2E\`, which \`grep\` shows has NEVER been written by any rung (the define and ONE READ, \`entry_storage.c:4233\`), and which the driver leaves alone because \`sdhci_prepare_data\` writes it only for a data command or \`MMC_RSP_BUSY\` and every command here is data-less. **THE ACT IS ONE BYTE STORE, VALUE \`0x03\` = 5,321.6 us, RAISED BEFORE CMD2 AND PUT BACK AFTER IT AND BEFORE CMD3** - the first repair this ladder has had rather than another measurement, and the only rung whose cells can be WRONG about a number instead of merely uninformative. **THE VALUE'S TWO ENDS ARE BOTH ASSERTED AT COMPILE TIME**: 0x01 is the floor (0x00 would write back the byte it found and be a no-op wearing a rung number) and 0x0E is the register's own maximum, while the two ends that matter RUNNING are 795 section 5's extrapolated 1,048.2 us arrival - which 0x03 clears by 5.08x, the per-bit rate ASSUMED and named - and the driver's own 1.200 s poll bound, which 0x03 stays 225x under so that the device timeout cannot hide behind the ladder's own give-up. **FOUR ROWS, AND THE FIRST IS LARGER THAN EVERY ROW BEFORE IT ON THIS LADDER**: \`_cid_complete = 1\` with any of \`_cid_resp0\` / \`_cid_raw2\` / \`_cid_raw3\` / \`_cid_resp1..3\` off its nine-arm value (\`_cid_raw0..3\` = \`0x0040ff80 / 0x80000000 / 0 / 0\`, \`_cid_resp0..3\` = \`0x40ff8080 / 0 / 0 / 0\`, byte-identical across nine arms) is **THE CID TAKEN**, 793 section 1's row 1a; \`_cid_complete = 1\` with the pattern unchanged is 793 section 5's fifth row on an arm where the bound is not the suspect; **\`ERR | TIMEOUT\` again at a LONGER tick count is the row that refutes 795 section 5's arithmetic and measures by how much**; and \`ERR | CRC\` returning refutes 795 section 2 and puts the immediate CRC back on the block independent of the bound. **THE REPAIR IS VISIBLE IN THE WINDOW'S OWN KEYS OR NOT AT ALL**: \`_tout_was\` is expected \`0\` (the reading that says nothing before this arm ever set the register), \`_tout_held = 3\` is the readback, \`_tout_wrote_back = 0\` and \`_tout_readback = 0\` are the restore - and **\`_tout_was = _tout_held = 0\` is the one failure the rest of the log cannot show**, because every other cell would read exactly as rung 31's did. **AND CMD3 IS DELIBERATELY LEFT AT THE RESET BOUND**: its 48-bit response fits inside 665.2 us, so it is the independent test of 795 section 6's protocol claim, and a window covering CMD3 would answer that question by helping CMD3 too. **A perfect CID here still does not move the ladder one command closer to a mount**: 794 measured the image's whole command vocabulary is CMD0-CMD3 with no CMD9 define, \`st_cmd_path()\` called once, and NO DATA PATH - so the distance to 「挂载存储」 is TWO frontiers, this bit AND the breadth gap. **THE GOAL IS NOT MET** - no transfer completes, no filesystem is reached and no mount is made - so **TWRP-to-storage STAYS WITHHELD**. **AN ARM IS ARMED AND NOT PRESSED AND THE PRESS IS THE OPERATOR'S**: rung 32 is \`armed-storage-c1f89600\`, parked at \`out/stage90/frozen/armed-storage-c1f89600/\`, its park verified 11 file(s) against \`records/revert-set.txt\`, and its value-30 containment measured at TEN OF ELEVEN MEMBERS byte-identical to the spent rung-31 park \`armed-storage-f9613649\`."
    rung_para 33 " **THIS RUNG IS A CONDITION AND NOT A BODY, AND IT IS THE ONE 803 NAMED AS THE SEPARATE RUNG THE LADDER OWED.** \`entry_storage.c\`'s CMD2 gate tested \`(c1.resp & ST_MMC_CARD_BUSY) == 0\` - THE PROBE's response - and now tests \`op_busy != 0\` - THE LOOP's result. **THE OLD CONDITION IS NOT BACKWARDS; IT IS READING THE WRONG WORD**: \`mmc_send_op_cond\` returns after ONE CMD1 by the driver's own design (\`mmc_ops.c:148-150\`'s \`if (ocr == 0) break;\`), so the probe's word is what a card that has not finished power-up answers - the OCR with bit 31 CLEAR - and \`== 0\` is TRUE, so the old gate PASSES. **It fires on the one reading that means \"come back later\" and passes on the reading that means \"not ready yet\"**, which is why \`_cid_gated\` read 0 on every arm from rung 16 through rung 32 and why all nine put CMD2 and CMD3 on the bus at a card that was not listening. \`mmc_ops.c:157\`'s \`if (cmd.resp[0] & MMC_CARD_BUSY) break;\` - the loop leaves when bit 31 SETS - is what \`op_busy\` is, and 803 measured both conditions true on one boot (\`_cmd1_resp = 0x40ff8080\` against \`_opcond_last_resp = 0xc0ff8080\`). **SO THIS REPAIR IS EXPECTED TO CHANGE NOTHING ON THIS CARD**, and its rows are about the repair: \`_cid_gate_word\` (the word the gate tested, read out of the LOOP's struct) and \`_cid_gate_busy\` (the test's result beside its source) are published on BOTH paths, so \`_cid_gated = 0\` with \`_cid_gate_busy = 1\` and the word off \`_cmd1_resp\` by exactly the busy bit is row 1, and \`_cid_gated = 1\` with reason 2 would be the first arm able to say the card's readiness is not reproducible boot to boot. **THE BUILD CLAUSE IS THE READING, NOT THIS SENTENCE**: \`xnu_entry_804\` reads three numbers out of the LINKED IMAGE in the window between \`st_op_cond_arg\`'s call and \`st_all_send_cid\`'s - sign-conditioned branches **0** against the spent park's **1** (\`bge\` at 8000eea8, the branch that PASSES when the card says it is NOT ready), loads from the PROBE's word **0** against **1** (slot \`[sp, #188]\`, derived from the value \`st_op_cond_arg\` is handed), and loads from the LOOP's struct **1** against **0** (base \`sp+224\`, derived from the address \`st_op_cond_loop\` is handed) - and both slots are DERIVED and not typed, so a frame that shifts moves the numbers with it. **THE CLAUSE REFUSED IN SILENCE TWICE BEFORE IT PRINTED A NUMBER**: a bare \`(( )) &&\` as the last command of a \`while\` body returns 1 when the comparison is false and this script runs \`set -e\`, and \`x=\$(... | grep ...)\` fails the same way when grep matches nothing - \`grep -c\` exits 1 WHEN THE COUNT IS ZERO, which is this clause's GOOD case. Every pipeline now carries \`|| true\`. **THE GOAL IS NOT MET** - no transfer completes, no filesystem is reached and no mount is made - so **TWRP-to-storage STAYS WITHHELD**, and **AN ARM IS ARMED AND NOT PRESSED AND THE PRESS IS THE OPERATOR'S**: rung 34 is \`armed-storage-7341f5f6\`, parked at \`out/stage90/frozen/armed-storage-7341f5f6/\`, its park verified 11 file(s) against \`records/revert-set.txt\`, and its value-32 containment measured at TEN OF ELEVEN MEMBERS byte-identical to the spent rung-33 park \`armed-storage-ce2f589c\`."
