    rung_para 34 " **THIS RUNG IS THE DRIVER'S FIRST COMMAND ABOVE CMD3: CMD9, \`SEND_CSD\` (mmc.h:38, \`ac [31:16] RCA R2\`), which is mmc.c:1420's \`mmc_send_csd(card, card->raw_csd)\` - the statement immediately after mmc.c:1409's \`mmc_set_relative_addr\`.** It is the ladder's SECOND 136-bit response and its FIRST with a non-zero argument: \`st_send_csd\` puts the driver's own word \`0x0909\` on the bus with \`ST_MMC_RCA_1\` and \`ST_MMC_RSP_R2\`. **AND ITS ARGUMENT IS \`card->rca << 16\` WITH \`card->rca = 1\` ASSIGNED BY THE DRIVER ITSELF (mmc.c:1400) - AN MMC CARD DOES NOT RETURN AN RCA TO THE HOST.** CMD3's response is R1 (mmc.h:32), 32 bits of card status: \`R1_CURRENT_STATE\` is bits 12:9 and \`R1_READY_FOR_DATA\` is bit 8, and there is no RCA field in it at ANY offset (an SD card returns one in R6, and even there the field is bits 31:16). **So the value this ladder's archive read as \"RCA 0x0500\" out of \`_nidx_resp = 0x00000500\` was read out of a field that does not exist**, and that same word under the vendor's own two macros is \`R1_READY_FOR_DATA\` set with \`R1_CURRENT_STATE = 2\` - and 2 is \`R1_STATE_IDENT\` (mmc.h:149), the state a card is in AFTER CMD2 and BEFORE a CMD3 it has ACCEPTED. \`_nidx_state\` says 2 in the committed rung-34 capture. **SO THE FRONTIER THIS ARM MEETS IS NOT CMD9's MECHANISM BUT THAT NO ARM HAS YET HAD A CMD3 THE CARD TOOK**, and CMD9 is legal in STBY and TRAN and not in IDENT. **THE PRECONDITION IS THEREFORE PUBLISHED AS A CELL RATHER THAN ASSUMED**: \`_csd_pre_state\`, \`_csd_pre_ready\` and \`_csd_pre_illegal\` are RESPONSE 0x10 read BETWEEN CMD3 and CMD9 - a moment no rung has read at, which is rung 18's own shape (\`st_resp_before\`) - so a press that finds the card in IDENT says so in the same log that reports what CMD9 did with it, and \`_csd_pre_state = 3\` or \`4\` is the reading that says the card was listening. **THE FOUR WORDS ARE DECODED WITH THE VENDOR'S OWN OFFSETS** (\`mmc_decode_csd\`, mmc.c:147-196 over \`UNSTUFF_BITS\`): \`_csd_structure\` is \`UNSTUFF_BITS(resp,126,2)\` and \`_csd_mmca_vsn\` is \`UNSTUFF_BITS(resp,122,4)\`, so **the values to check are \`structure\` non-zero and \`mmca_vsn\` 4** - and the rung-35 PRESS MEASURED them as **3 and 4**: \`mmc.c:159\` rejects only \`0\`, \`{1,2}\` is the SD family's reading of a shared field name, and an eMMC 4.41 card reads 3. **819 CORRECTED THIS SENTENCE**: it first said they \"must read **1** and **4**\", and it reached that from \`mmc.c:110\`, which is inside \`mmc_decode_cid\` and switches on \`cid->mmca_vsn\` - a DIFFERENT switch variable in a DIFFERENT decoder from \`mmc_decode_csd\`'s, which is \`structure\` at \`mmc.c:158-163\`. The pair is now a build refusal, \`ST_CSD_STRUCTURE_IS_CSD\` over 0/1/2/3, so a later rung cannot narrow it back. The two values this image did not supply and could not have chosen are 3 and 4, which is the same free cross-check the CID's \`serial\` gave against \`ro.serialno\` (0x4a2fe00b; 811 section 4). \`_csd_capacity_blocks\` carries 12-bit \`C_SIZE\` and is EXPECTED to be a placeholder on a 16 GB part (mmc.c:201's own note about the \"magic\" size), because the real capacity is in the EXT_CSD - which is 809's wall, CMD8, named one rung early by arithmetic. **THE BUILD CLAUSE IS THE READING, NOT THIS SENTENCE**: \`xnu_entry_812\` reads \`st_send_csd\` out of the LINKED IMAGE - r0=**9**, r1=**65536**, r2=**7** immediately before its \`bl\` to \`st_send_command\`, and its device accesses IN PROGRAM ORDER as the four \`RESPONSE\` words at 0x1C, 0x18, 0x14, 0x10 (WORD 3 FIRST, sdhci.c:1167's \`(3-i)*4\`) then the three CRC bytes at 0x1B, 0x17, 0x13 (each ONE BELOW its own word) **with NO byte at 0x0F**, because the vendor's \`if (i != 3)\` gives the last word none - plus the \`INT_ENABLE\` window, \`SIGNAL_ENABLE\`, \`INT_STATUS\` and \`PRESENT_STATE\`, an EMPTY image side, the call count 1 from \`st_cmd_path\`, and the \`f9824910:ldr=2\` count that proves the precondition read and word 0 were NOT commoned into one load. **THE GOAL IS NOT MET** - no transfer completes, no filesystem is reached and no mount is made - so **TWRP-to-storage STAYS WITHHELD**, and **AN ARM IS ARMED AND NOT PRESSED AND THE PRESS IS THE OPERATOR'S**: rung 35 is \`${SET:-<unresolved>}\`, parked at \`out/stage90/frozen/${SET:-<unresolved>}/\` with eleven members, and its containment is measured member by member against the WITHDRAWN park \`armed-storage-6cd6fae8\` - **two of eleven byte-identical** (\`stage90-build-config.txt\` and \`stage90_fixture.macho\`, the two that neither embed nor list the entry image) and nine moving, which is what a step that changes EMITTED CODE looks like; \`xnu_arm_entry-config.txt\` differs in exactly one line and \`xnu_arm_entry-sources.txt\` in exactly two of its 28."
    # **819: THE RUNG-36 PARAGRAPH, AND IT MUST NOT BE FOLDED INTO THE RUNG-35 TEXT ABOVE IT.**
    # That one narrates CMD9 and this narrates the driver's NEXT command; rung 27's reason for a
    # per-rung paragraph applies twice over here, because these two rungs also differ in KIND - one
